    "created_at": "2023-05-04T17:31:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-04T17:31:15Z",
    "body": "@annevk `2023-02-09` and `2023-02-09T22:00:00.000Z` values do match the type of control - they are both ISO date strings. Seems like date input should support both. Maybe my expectations were set by MDN mentioning the \"date is formatted according to ISO8601\", which for anyone who's worked with dates can be more than just yyyy-mm-dd. I think I'll suggest an edit over there...\r\n\r\nI realize we're talking HTML here, but what's more is this means `dateInput.value = new Date().toISOString()` doesn't work as well. That's very unexpected and disappointing for developers. And JS doesn't have a function for parsing out the date portion, you have to slice the string.\r\n\r\nI think this is a valid critique of the current spec and should be reconsidered.",
